<leaf id="0x4c780002">
  <desc>Linux-defined synthetic CPU bug flags</desc>
  <text>
    This is a Linux-defined synthetic CPUID leaf, where "Linux" is a virtual vendor
    mirroring hardware vendors like AMD and Intel.  The leaf ID prefix 0x4c78 is
    for Linux, in its shorthand ASCII form "Lx".

    The bit listing mirrors what Linux defines in its synthetic X86_BUG words.
    The listed CPU bug bits are expected to be set in stone, and new bits must be
    filled in that order: subleaf 0 (EAX->EDX), subleaf 1 (EAX->EDX), and so on.
  </text>
  <vendors>
    <vendor>Linux</vendor>
  </vendors>
  <subleaf id="0">
